  "cause_evidence": {
    "strong_observations": [
      "Raw has IN/OUT/REC for sequence0,1,2, then IN for sequence3, followed by FATAL at original TB60 trailing token in finish_file. No earlier END required, tuple, latency or handshake fatal is reported.",
      "For MODE0, TB188 loads and drives every input frame, then TB189 calls finish_file(input_fd) before offer_terminal/wait(all_outputs_done). This explains why fourth IN exists but fourth OUT/REC is absent when the input-tail check fails.",
      "Original TB59 requires a successful END token; original TB60 performs a second %s scan and requires z==-1. The observed trailing token fatal establishes that this second scan did not satisfy the expected -1 comparison.",
      "All23 original fixed text files, including actual tested p0_main input.txt and expected.txt, end in exact END LF bytes. The current source, tested copy, archive and preserved hash maps agree. There is no stored extra token after END in the failed input.",
      "Retained compiled P0.vvp finish_file task has the two original fscanf calls at source59/60, compares the second32-bit result against4294967295, and emits the matching trailing token fatal. This rules out a mismatched repaired TB image."
    ],
    "supported_narrow_diagnosis": "The failure is strongly localized to the original END-tail fscanf EOF-return assumption on the pinned Icarus path. A runtime EOF/whitespace behavior mismatch is the leading explanation; the actual bytes do not support a real extra trailing token in the sealed fixture.",
    "not_proven": [
      "The raw does not print the second fscanf return value or token. In particular, return0 is plausible but is not directly measured and is not claimed as fact.",
      "No controlled reproduction or instrumented run was performed. This audit does not prove a general Icarus defect or that the replacement will pass all later checks.",
      "Three completed REC records and partial fourth input are useful diagnostic evidence, not a completed simulation PASS or a basis to carry the failed simulation."
    ]
  },
